  "suggestion": "Transform the interface into a 'Digital Workbench' aesthetic. Give the cube stickers a distinct material finish—matte plastic with subtle edge wear or glossy vinyl—to create a tactile focal point. Replace the floating, generic UI panels with a 'HUD' style that feels attached to the cube's geometry, perhaps using a monospaced, technical font for the timer to evoke a stopwatch. Introduce a dynamic, moody lighting setup (e.g., a spotlight from above) to cast real-time shadows and emphasize the 3D volume. Use a high-contrast, electric color palette for the stickers against a deep, textured charcoal background to make the colors pop. Finally, add a subtle 'breathing' animation to the cube when idle to suggest it is a living, waiting mechanism."
